# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section uses a 10-site system to illustrate the AQC-Tensor workflow step by step. We simulate the dynamics of a 10-site XXZ spin chain, a widely studied model for examining spin interactions and magnetic properties.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Bahagian ini menggunakan sistem 10-tapak untuk menggambarkan aliran kerja AQC-Tensor langkah demi langkah. Kita mensimulasikan dinamik rantai spin XXZ 10-tapak, model yang dikaji secara meluas untuk mengkaji interaksi spin dan sifat magnetik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{XXZ} = \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} J_{i,(i+1)}\\left(X_i X_{(i+1)}+Y_i Y_{(i+1)}+ 2\\cdot Z_i Z_{(i+1)} \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian adalah seperti berikut:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{XXZ} = \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} J_{i,(i+1)}\\left(X_i X_{(i+1)}+Y_i Y_{(i+1)}+ 2\\cdot Z_i Z_{(i+1)} \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J_{i,(i+1)}$ is a random coefficient for edge $(i, i+1)$ and $L=10$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $J_{i,(i+1)}$ adalah pekali rawak untuk tepi $(i, i+1)$ dan $L=10$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this step, we:\n"
"1. Define the Hamiltonian, observable, and initial state.\n"
"2. Compute the exact expectation value classically for later comparison.\n"
"3. Generate a high-accuracy Trotter circuit (the AQC target) and compress it into a low-depth ansatz using AQC-Tensor.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah ini, kita:\n"
"1. Takrifkan Hamiltonian, boleh cerap, dan keadaan awal.\n"
"2. Kira nilai jangkaan yang tepat secara klasik untuk perbandingan kemudian.\n"
"3. Jana litar Trotter berketepatan tinggi (sasaran AQC) dan mampatkannya kepada ansatz berkedalaman rendah menggunakan AQC-Tensor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the Hamiltonian, observable, and initial state {#set-up-the-hamiltonian-observable-and-initial-state}"
msgstr "Sediakan Hamiltonian, boleh cerap, dan keadaan awal {#set-up-the-hamiltonian-observable-and-initial-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/527dbada-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/527dbada-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the exact expectation value {#compute-the-exact-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Kira nilai jangkaan yang tepat {#compute-the-exact-expectation-value}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a system of this size, we can compute the exact time-evolved expectation value directly using matrix exponentiation. This serves as our ground truth for evaluating the AQC circuit's accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Untuk sistem bersaiz ini, kita boleh mengira nilai jangkaan yang berevolusi masa dengan tepat secara langsung menggunakan pendaraban eksponen matriks. Ini menjadi rujukan kebenaran kita untuk menilai ketepatan litar AQC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the AQC target circuit {#generate-the-aqc-target-circuit}"
msgstr "Jana litar sasaran AQC {#generate-the-aqc-target-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now construct the Trotter circuit that will serve as the AQC target. This circuit uses many Trotter steps (32) for high accuracy. Because it will only be simulated classically as an MPS&mdash;not executed on hardware&mdash;the large depth is not a concern.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini membina litar Trotter yang akan menjadi sasaran AQC. Litar ini menggunakan banyak langkah Trotter (32) untuk ketepatan yang tinggi. Kerana ia hanya akan disimulasikan secara klasik sebagai MPS&mdash;bukan dilaksanakan pada perkakasan&mdash;kedalaman yang besar bukan satu kebimbangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate an ansatz, initial parameters, subsequent circuit, and a baseline circuit {#generate-an-ansatz-initial-parameters-subsequent-circuit-and-a-baseline-circuit}"
msgstr "Jana ansatz, parameter awal, litar seterusnya, dan litar garis dasar {#generate-an-ansatz-initial-parameters-subsequent-circuit-and-a-baseline-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we construct a \"good\" circuit with the same evolution time as the AQC target but far fewer Trotter steps (only one). We pass this circuit to `generate_ansatz_from_circuit`, which returns:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita membina litar \"baik\" dengan masa evolusi yang sama seperti sasaran AQC tetapi dengan langkah Trotter yang jauh lebih sedikit (hanya satu). Kita menghantar litar ini ke `generate_ansatz_from_circuit`, yang mengembalikan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A general, parametrized **ansatz** circuit with the same two-qubit connectivity.\n"
msgstr "Litar **ansatz** berparameter umum dengan ketersambungan dua-qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Initial parameters** that reproduce the input circuit when plugged into the ansatz.\n"
msgstr "**Parameter awal** yang menghasilkan semula litar input apabila dimasukkan ke dalam ansatz.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also construct:\n"
"- A **subsequent circuit** with one Trotter step that will be appended (uncompressed) after the AQC-optimized portion, following the approach in the [AQC-Tensor initial state tutorial](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/tutorials/01_initial_state_aqc.html).\n"
"- A **baseline Trotter circuit** using four Trotter steps over the full evolution time (`aqc_evolution_time + subsequent_evolution_time`). This serves as the comparison: it represents what you would run on hardware without AQC. The AQC ansatz (3 compressed steps + 1 uncompressed step) achieves better accuracy at lower depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga membina:\n"
"- **Litar seterusnya** dengan satu langkah Trotter yang akan dilampirkan (tidak dimampatkan) selepas bahagian yang dioptimumkan oleh AQC, mengikuti pendekatan dalam [tutorial keadaan awal AQC-Tensor](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/tutorials/01_initial_state_aqc.html).\n"
"- **Litar Trotter garis dasar** menggunakan empat langkah Trotter merentasi jumlah masa evolusi (`aqc_evolution_time + subsequent_evolution_time`). Ini berfungsi sebagai perbandingan: ia mewakili apa yang akan anda jalankan pada perkakasan tanpa AQC. Ansatz AQC (3 langkah termampat + 1 langkah tidak termampat) mencapai ketepatan yang lebih baik pada kedalaman yang lebih rendah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/78f2665e-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/78f2665e-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up tensor network simulation and build the target MPS {#set-up-tensor-network-simulation-and-build-the-target-mps}"
msgstr "Sediakan simulasi rangkaian tensor dan bina MPS sasaran {#set-up-tensor-network-simulation-and-build-the-target-mps}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use the [quimb](https://github.com/jcmgray/quimb) matrix-product state (MPS) circuit simulator, with JAX providing automatic differentiation for the gradient-based optimization. We then build an MPS representation of the target state and evaluate the starting fidelity between the initial ansatz and the target. As the problem instance is a relatively small example, the starting fidelity starts off quite high.\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan simulator litar keadaan produk matriks (MPS) [quimb](https://github.com/jcmgray/quimb), dengan JAX menyediakan pembezaan automatik untuk pengoptimuman berasaskan kecerunan. Kita kemudian membina perwakilan MPS bagi keadaan sasaran dan menilai kesetiaan awal antara ansatz awal dan sasaran. Memandangkan contoh masalah ini adalah contoh yang agak kecil, kesetiaan awal bermula agak tinggi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize the ansatz parameters {#optimize-the-ansatz-parameters}"
msgstr "Optimumkan parameter ansatz {#optimize-the-ansatz-parameters}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We minimize the `MaximizeStateFidelity` cost function using the L-BFGS-B optimizer. The optimizer iteratively adjusts the ansatz parameters to maximize the fidelity between the ansatz circuit and the target MPS.\n"
msgstr "Kita meminimumkan fungsi kos `MaximizeStateFidelity` menggunakan pengoptimum L-BFGS-B. Pengoptimum ini menyesuaikan parameter ansatz secara berulang untuk memaksimumkan kesetiaan antara litar ansatz dan MPS sasaran.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the final AQC circuit {#assemble-the-final-aqc-circuit}"
msgstr "Kumpulkan litar AQC akhir {#assemble-the-final-aqc-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the optimized parameters in hand, we bind them to the ansatz and then append the subsequent (uncompressed) Trotter step. The resulting circuit has the depth of a single compressed Trotter step plus one uncompressed step, but the compressed portion approximates the accuracy of 32 Trotter steps.\n"
msgstr "Dengan parameter yang dioptimumkan, kita ikatkan kepada ansatz dan kemudian lampirkan langkah Trotter seterusnya (tidak dimampatkan). Litar yang terhasil mempunyai kedalaman satu langkah Trotter termampat ditambah satu langkah tidak termampat, tetapi bahagian yang dimampatkan menghampiri ketepatan 32 langkah Trotter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/e09e40de-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/e09e40de-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this small-scale example, we use a fake backend (`FakeKyiv`) to simulate hardware execution locally. We transpile both the AQC-optimized circuit (`aqc_final_circuit`) and the baseline Trotter circuit (`baseline_circuit`, four Trotter steps over the full evolution time, no AQC) to the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA), with `optimization_level=3` to further reduce circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh skala kecil ini, kita menggunakan backend palsu (`FakeKyiv`) untuk mensimulasikan pelaksanaan perkakasan secara tempatan. Kita mentranspilkan kedua-dua litar yang dioptimumkan oleh AQC (`aqc_final_circuit`) dan litar Trotter garis dasar (`baseline_circuit`, empat langkah Trotter merentasi jumlah masa evolusi, tanpa AQC) kepada seni bina set arahan (ISA) backend, dengan `optimization_level=3` untuk mengurangkan lagi kedalaman litar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use the [`EstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) primitive with the fake backend to run both the AQC-optimized circuit and the baseline Trotter circuit, measuring the ZZ observable for each.\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan primitif [`EstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) dengan backend palsu untuk menjalankan kedua-dua litar yang dioptimumkan oleh AQC dan litar Trotter garis dasar, mengukur observable ZZ bagi setiap satu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Proses pasca dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We extract the expectation values from both runs and compare them to the exact result. The baseline Trotter circuit shows what we would get without AQC at the same circuit depth, while the AQC circuit demonstrates the improvement from tensor-network optimization.\n"
msgstr "Kita mengekstrak nilai jangkaan daripada kedua-dua pelaksanaan dan membandingkannya dengan hasil yang tepat. Litar Trotter garis dasar menunjukkan apa yang kita dapat tanpa AQC pada kedalaman litar yang sama, manakala litar AQC menunjukkan penambahbaikan daripada pengoptimuman rangkaian tensor.\n"

